WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:12.230
[TEXT: I swear to God and before the Colombian
people, to defend Colombia’s laws and Constitution.]

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:17.390
On August 7th 2018, Iván Duque Márquez was
sworn in as president of Colombia.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:21.520
His campaign promise was straightforward:
to get the country in shape and ready for

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.210
a rapid development process.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:31.279
Enough time has passed since Iván Duque rose
to power for VISUALPOLITIK to ask some questions:

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:33.899
What is the true strategic plan of Duque’s
government?

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:36.749
That is, how does he want to transform Colombia?

00:00:36.749 --> 00:00:37.999
Can he achieve this goal?

00:00:37.999 --> 00:00:47.370
What could be the legacy of his passage through
Casa Nariño – the Colombian White House?

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:58.229
Listen up.

00:00:58.229 --> 00:01:03.670
(INTRO)

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:08.070
With almost 50 million inhabitants, Colombia
is the second-most populous country in South

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.070
America.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.219
But it is, above all, a very, very complicated
country:

00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:14.810
On the one hand, there’s the problem of
the guerrillas and drug trafficking, which

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:17.450
happens to be one of the country’s biggest
industries.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:22.229
To give you an idea, Colombia produces no
less than 70% of all the white powder on the

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:23.229
planet.

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:24.229
70%!

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:29.880
Of course, as you can imagine, behind this
huge business that moves thousands and billions

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.760
of dollars every year, there are some powerful
criminal organizations.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:38.210
Organizations that are willing to control
their territory come hell or high water.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.329
That’s precisely why violence rates remain
so high.

00:01:41.329 --> 00:01:47.109
(AUDIO: Colombia: homicides increased in 2018
due to violence after the FARC’s disarmament-

00:01:47.109 --> 00:01:52.920
According to the country's forensic authority,
there were 12,130 homicides last year, 6.7%

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.499
more than in 2017.

00:01:54.499 --> 00:01:55.499
- DW)

00:01:55.499 --> 00:01:58.490
And the violence isn’t limited to drug deals
gone bad or territorial disputes.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:02.749
In the last three years alone, it’s estimated
that more than 500 community activists and

00:02:02.749 --> 00:02:07.189
leaders lost their lives at the hands of these
groups; and about 200,000 people have been

00:02:07.189 --> 00:02:09.070
displaced from their homes.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:12.100
And it doesn't end there.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:16.230
The ELN, a far leftist guerrilla group – also
linked to drug trafficking – continues to

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.230
operate;

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:21.220
(AUDIO: 21/01/2019 The ELN guerrilla claims
the attack on the police academy that caused

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:22.340
more than 20 deaths.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.340
RTVE)

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.620
What’s more, about 3,000 former members
of FARC may have taken up their weapons again;

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.970
and Coca plantations are at a record high.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:37.450
(AUDIO: Coca crops in Colombia reached an
all-time high in 2017 with 171,000 hectares.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.110
UN News)

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:42.300
As if all these problems weren’t enough,
Colombia has recently had to deal with the

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:47.190
arrival of hundreds of thousands of Venezuelans
fleeing Nicolás Maduro’s despotic regime.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:53.660
It’s estimated that approximately 1.5 million
Venezuelans already live in Colombia.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:57.700
One thing that is very positive is the Colombian
solidarity that’s been witnessed.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.660
The problem is that this influx of people
also puts enormous pressure on stability and

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.660
public resources.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.470
Ok, so let's say this is the downside.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:09.620
But it’s not all bad news in Colombia.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:18.110
You see, despite all the continuing problems,
such as drug trafficking, guerrillas, paramilitary

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.722
groups, violence, corruption... the country
has actually registered an average economic

00:03:21.722 --> 00:03:27.010
growth of 3.8% per year over the last 40 years;
The middle class has grown and the country

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.970
hasn’t suffered any hyperinflation.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:33.390
And, don’t think this is normal because
it’s anything but.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.870
Don’t forget that we’re talking about
South America.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:40.510
In that same period, Peru, Bolivia, Argentina,
Ecuador, Brazil and Venezuela have undergone

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.470
hyperinflation processes.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:49.780
In other words, we could almost say that Colombia
is a model of stability.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:53.760
However Colombian President Iván Duque doesn’t
quite agree.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:59.010
(AUDIO: Colombian President Iván Duque affirms
that he isn’t satisfied with the more than

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:04.290
3% growth that the Colombian economy is expected
to have this year and intends to “push the

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.452
country to grow by more than 5% annually”.

00:04:05.452 --> 00:04:06.452
ElPaís.com.co)

00:04:06.452 --> 00:04:07.452
[TEXT: And of course, I’m not satisfied,
I’m not saying that we should grow by more

00:04:07.452 --> 00:04:08.452
than 3% and that’d be enough, no!

00:04:08.452 --> 00:04:09.452
We want more, and I state it like this: Colombia
is a country that has a per capita income

00:04:09.452 --> 00:04:10.452
of almost $ 7,000.

00:04:10.452 --> 00:04:11.452
We are an OECD country, the other OECD countries
have per capita incomes of more than $ 30,000,

00:04:11.452 --> 00:04:12.452
so my question is, how long would it take
Colombia to reach that level of per capita

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.452
income?

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:14.452
100 years growing at 1% or 20 years growing
at above 5%.

00:04:14.452 --> 00:04:16.519
What we need to do is get the country to grow
at above 5%.

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:19.790
Make decisions to get that sustained growth
and that’s what we are doing.]

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.880
Yes, the Colombian president has set a goal
of 5%.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.250
Now, will they be able to achieve it?

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:29.120
How will they go about it?

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.370
It seems complicated considering the scenario
described, doesn’t it?

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:33.540
Well, you know what?

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.040
We can’t say if he’ll be successful or
not, but the important thing is that this

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:42.120
government has a plan – which, unfortunately,
doesn’t seem to happen so often these days,

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.680
right President Macri?

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:49.250
And it’s a plan that doesn’t look too
bad, and which we can summarise into three

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.530
main points.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:54.460
Listen up.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:59.160
(FLEEING LATIN AMERICAN TAXATION)

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:04.690
This may come as a surprise, but in general,
Latin American countries’ tax systems have

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:07.060
one common characteristic:

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:10.310
They have the highest corporate taxes on the
planet.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:13.800
Want an example?

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.120
Listen up.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:20.250
The inability of the government to raise money
from living, flesh and blood people, has made

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:28.510
them tax the productive system voraciously.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:32.150
This is quite the opposite of the example
set by Nordic countries, and they are often

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:33.350
held up as a benchmark.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:37.840
And, if Latin America is usually a disaster
in this field, Colombia is the worst of the

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:38.840
worst.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.300
But okay, some of you may be wondering, Simon,
how much worse?

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.660
1 point, 2 points?

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:45.910
Well, not even close.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:55.180
To give you an idea, according to the latest
Doing Business report from the World Bank,

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:59.820
the effective tax rate on Colombian companies,
that is, if we consider all the taxes that

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:03.060
a company is obliged to pay: local, national,
labor, corporate…

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:11.890
Then it turns out that Colombian companies
face an average rate of a whopping 71.9%.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:16.650
71.9% of the company’s commercial profit,
that is the difference between income and

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:21.350
expenses without taking taxes into account,
goes directly into the Public Administration’s

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:22.350
pocket.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:26.960
To give you an idea, when a Colombian company
buys a machine, VAT cannot be fully deducted

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:27.960
for that purchase.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.230
And companies have to pay taxes even if they
are losing money.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.230
Crazy, isn’t it?

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:40.040
And obviously, all this has consequences:

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:44.520
Such high taxes on the productive sector affect
the Colombian economy’s ability to be competitive.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:50.850
And on top of this we have to add the exhausting
and tedious bureaucracy that is so typical

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.290
in Latin American countries.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:56.540
Basically, under these conditions it would
be easier to win a fight against a professional

00:06:56.540 --> 00:07:00.490
boxer like Andrew Cancio or Floyd Mayweather,
than it would be to start a business that

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:01.490
works.

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:05.840
Surely now you understand why Latin American
countries generally have low investment levels,

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:09.250
low export levels and a lot, a lot of informal
economies.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:17.030
(AUDIO: 05/2017: Latin America’s informal
economy surpasses that of sub-Saharan Africa

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:18.350
for the first time.

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:20.630
World Economic Forum)

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:26.590
In fact, it’s estimated that more than 54%
of Colombian companies aren’t operating

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.720
within official guidelines.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:33.030
And of course, an informal company can’t
access large contracts, bank financing or

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.200
have legal security.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:35.960
They just can’t grow.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.370
Well, addressing this situation is precisely
the first major point of Ivan Duque's plan.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:44.310
In fact, at the end of last year he got the
Congress of the Republic of Colombia to approve

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:45.880
a comprehensive tax reform.

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:47.780
His tax reform.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:53.160
Basically, the reform aims to reduce the tax
requirements of Colombian companies by slightly

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:59.420
increasing taxes on higher personal incomes,
for example to people who earn more than $120,000

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:01.400
and who currently pay low taxes.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.790
The reform will also increase VAT collection.

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:08.390
So, with the new reform, corporate income
tax will be progressively reduced from 33

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:13.900
to 30%; some additional taxes will disappear
and a simplified single-tax system with very

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:18.430
low rates will be created to encourage the
formalization and growth of small businesses.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:19.430
[TEXT: With a 100% discount of VAT paid on
capital goods and a 50% discount of the ICA

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.430
and the gradual dismantling of the presumptive
income.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.430
In addition to a simple regime that differentiates
rates, especially for fledgling companies,

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.430
is having effects.]

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.430
And that's not all.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.760
In addition, the reform has also created tax
incentives for entrepreneurs, for investments

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:30.210
in large projects, investments in the tourism
sector and in the so-called orange economy.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:34.949
And yes, okay, this may seem controversial,
after all, why apply it to some sectors and

00:08:34.949 --> 00:08:35.949
not others?

00:08:35.949 --> 00:08:39.869
But at least it seems to be a step in the
right direction, doesn’t it?

00:08:39.869 --> 00:08:44.139
The problem, and perhaps what has made this
project so controversial, is that Duque is

00:08:44.139 --> 00:08:48.869
going to increase public spending significantly
and the government already has a high public

00:08:48.869 --> 00:08:49.869
deficit.

00:08:49.869 --> 00:08:53.819
So even though the measure means a reduction
of taxes in the medium term, the truth is

00:08:53.819 --> 00:08:58.350
that in the short term it implies increasing
them.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:02.579
That is, while the reductions are progressive
and will be applied gradually, the increases

00:09:02.579 --> 00:09:04.769
will be applied from the very beginning.

00:09:04.769 --> 00:09:08.399
For example, a temporary surcharge on bank
profits.

00:09:08.399 --> 00:09:10.459
And this hasn’t been popular at all.

00:09:10.459 --> 00:09:14.240
But still – and you know that on VisualPolitik
we don't like tax increases at all – we

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:16.639
think the change is a step in the right direction.

00:09:16.639 --> 00:09:21.149
Latin America in general and Colombia, in
particular, have to treat the productive sectors

00:09:21.149 --> 00:09:22.149
better.

00:09:22.149 --> 00:09:24.899
Latin America needs more companies, not more
taxes.

00:09:24.899 --> 00:09:28.970
Unfortunately, this reform has been declared
unconstitutional due to a formality.

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:32.329
Now the government has to get it approved
again in Congress.

00:09:32.329 --> 00:09:37.540
Could President Duque get it through?

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:45.269
(THE ORANGE ECONOMY)

00:09:45.269 --> 00:09:50.170
The second key point in Iván Duque's strategy
is to promote the so-called orange economy

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:54.490
with fiscal incentives, participatory loans,
venture capital and startup accelerators.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:56.300
Now let’s pause a second.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:59.910
Many of you, especially those who aren’t
Colombian, will be wondering, what on earth

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.250
is the orange economy?

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:07.149
Well, no, it has nothing to do with the fruit,
it’s an umbrella term for creative activities

00:10:07.149 --> 00:10:11.589
that are related to intellectual property:
music, design, audiovisual productions, YouTube

00:10:11.589 --> 00:10:15.559
channels, architecture, art, software design,
etcetera, etcetera.

00:10:15.559 --> 00:10:22.389
[TEXT: Zero, zero income tax for 7 years to
all new ventures in the creative and technological

00:10:22.389 --> 00:10:26.509
industries because these are the years where
those ventures take off.]

00:10:26.509 --> 00:10:31.139
Look, have you noticed that more and more
movies and series are being filmed in Colombia?

00:10:31.139 --> 00:10:34.910
Even more and more productions from platforms
such as Netflix or Amazon Prime are being

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:36.490
made in this country.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:38.170
And there’s a good reason for this.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:45.129
In 2012, Law 1556 was passed, which provides
significant tax breaks and aid to produce

00:10:45.129 --> 00:10:47.939
and shoot films and TV series in Colombia.

00:10:47.939 --> 00:10:51.970
That way, they not only sought to grow the
national film industry but also to foster

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.670
a better image of the country around the world.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:58.550
This resulted in a soaring number of productions
shot in Colombia.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:03.839
Well, now Iván Duque wants to do the same
with all the activities that make up this

00:11:03.839 --> 00:11:04.839
“orange economy”.

00:11:04.839 --> 00:11:07.579
And pay attention because this is serious
business.

00:11:07.579 --> 00:11:10.999
Today Colombia’s orange economy is almost
three times larger than the coffee industry

00:11:10.999 --> 00:11:13.970
and almost as big as the entire mining sector.

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:17.689
We’re talking about economic activities
whose worldwide trade grows at annual rates

00:11:17.689 --> 00:11:22.579
of 7% and whose value in 2015 exceeded 500
billion dollars.

00:11:22.579 --> 00:11:26.139
(AUDIO: “The orange economy is larger than
new oil.

00:11:26.139 --> 00:11:28.959
Oil reserves are limited but creativity is
unlimited.

00:11:28.959 --> 00:11:34.029
We have to know that the most important heritage
we have in a society is the talent of its

00:11:34.029 --> 00:11:35.029
people.”

00:11:35.029 --> 00:11:36.029
Ivan Duque)

00:11:36.029 --> 00:11:39.300
Well, in order to boost other ‘orange economy’
activities, the government is implementing

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:43.899
participatory financing plans, venture capital
initiatives, entrepreneurship centers and

00:11:43.899 --> 00:11:44.899
tax exemptions.

00:11:44.899 --> 00:11:46.379
So, will it work?

00:11:46.379 --> 00:11:49.720
Will the orange economy really be able to
transform Colombia?

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:51.720
Only time will tell, but, you know what?

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:58.139
This plan sounds pretty good.

00:11:58.139 --> 00:12:02.769
And the plan is different in that it is linked
to human capital and not just natural resources

00:12:02.769 --> 00:12:07.959
or large companies that have suspiciously
close ties to governments, which, unfortunately,

00:12:07.959 --> 00:12:10.699
is the norm in Latin America.

00:12:10.699 --> 00:12:11.999
But it doesn’t end there.

00:12:11.999 --> 00:12:19.249
We still have a third essential pillar in
this strategy.

00:12:19.249 --> 00:12:26.679
(THE NEW BETS)

00:12:26.679 --> 00:12:30.699
It isn’t strictly ​​Iván Duque’s
idea, but it looks like the new government

00:12:30.699 --> 00:12:34.160
has accepted it.

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:37.320
Colombia wants to become a big player in the
world market for medical cannabis.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:41.569
This is a sector that is literally growing
like weeds and is expected to become a market

00:12:41.569 --> 00:12:44.199
of almost 50 billion by 2025.

00:12:44.199 --> 00:12:47.790
And Colombia intends to have a slice of that
pie, more than 40%.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:52.179
We’re talking about a huge sector and a
considerable boost for the Colombian economy,

00:12:52.179 --> 00:12:55.189
especially for the economy in the poorest
rural areas.

00:12:55.189 --> 00:12:59.399
(AUDIO “It calls us to the possibility of
being very important worldwide players in

00:12:59.399 --> 00:13:05.100
terms of exports, estimates state that we
could effectively reach levels of US $6 billion

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:06.310
annually in exports”.

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:10.360
Saúl Pineda, Vice Minister of Business Development)

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:17.060
Well, along with the pointy green weeds, the
government’s other big gamble consists of

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:22.209
promoting fracking to increase oil production.

00:13:22.209 --> 00:13:26.710
So far four pilot projects have been approved
that could produce more than 400 thousand

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.889
barrels per day when fully operational.

00:13:28.889 --> 00:13:38.870
This would mean increasing Colombia's oil
production by almost 50%.

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:42.730
In conclusion, with all these measures and
with greater investment in infrastructure

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:47.499
and education, Ivan Duque’s government plans
to achieve its objective of raising Colombia's

00:13:47.499 --> 00:13:49.649
economic growth to above 5%.

00:13:49.649 --> 00:13:52.079
Will they achieve it?

00:13:52.079 --> 00:13:57.089
Here on VisualPolitik we’ll be watching
closely, but as things stand, it doesn’t

00:13:57.089 --> 00:13:58.089
look too bad.

00:13:58.089 --> 00:14:01.470
Of course, there are other issues yet to resolve
and which could generate several problems:

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:05.449
for example, the sharp increase in public
spending or the constant devaluation of the

00:14:05.449 --> 00:14:06.449
Colombian peso.

00:14:06.449 --> 00:14:10.350
And, of course, Duque’s government hasn’t
limited itself to act only in the economic

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:11.350
field.

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:12.350
What about drug-traffickers?

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:13.350
How can they improve security?

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.110
What are they doing in terms of foreign policy?

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:18.819
Well, we'll cover these topics in an upcoming
video here on this channel.

00:14:18.819 --> 00:14:23.699
So I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did, and don’t forget to

00:14:23.699 --> 00:14:25.420
subscribe for brand new videos.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.809
Don’t forget to check out our friends at
the Reconsider Media Podcast - they provided

